values ('c5d6e7f8-9a0b-4c66-9f56-6d7e8f9a0b66', 'introduction-to-the-humanities', 'Introduction to the Humanities', 'Introduction to the Humanities is a first-year course in the study of human meaning, expression, memory, value, and culture. Students read literature, examine philosophy, analyze visual art and architecture, listen to music, interpret performance, study history and religion, and investigate how language, media, power, and identity shape cultural life. The course emphasizes close reading, close looking, historical context, ethical reasoning, cross-cultural comparison, research literacy, and public communication.');

